From d7c39ba798f5d49b1f469811da3a86b6db97af1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gaia <build@heygaia.io>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 03:39:40 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] fix(js,cdp): window.open opens a real window, and only with
 user activation

window.open returned null and did nothing, so a page's popups (OAuth, "open
in new tab" flows, print views) never appeared and clients waiting for the new
target waited forever.

window.open now follows HTML's window open steps for a top-level page:
_self/_parent/_top navigate this page; any other target opens a new
top-level page in the opener's browser context, reported with
Target.targetCreated (with openerId) and Target.attachedToTarget, and loaded
through the connection's navigation path with its usual events; a named
target reuses the window this page opened under that name. The returned
window proxy can navigate (location) and close() its window, the parts that
cross pages. Like Chrome's popup blocker, opening needs transient user
activation: a trusted press, release or key press within the last five
seconds, consumed by the open; noopener/noreferrer return null.

Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tm2SNEJ42hMPiZ6cFb8Vih
